4. BROADER CLAIM ATTACHED DOWNSTREAM
-----------------------------------------------------------------
RETRIEVED (Wikipedia summary of contemporary media and later literature, cross-checked against paper claims):
- Contemporary media coverage (New York Times, USA Today, Boston Globe, Nature press materials, NSF release, April 1998) highlighted the finding that recent years were warmer than any since at least AD 1400 and the suggestion of greenhouse-gas dominance in the 20th century. Coverage often framed the result in the context of human influence questions. (Provenance: RETRIEVED from secondary summaries of 1998 coverage; exact contemporaneous quotes not re-fetched here.)

RETRIEVED (Wikipedia / secondary sources on IPCC use):
- MBH98 methodology and reconstruction underpinned the subsequent MBH99 extension (to AD 1000). IPCC Third Assessment Report (TAR, 2001) prominently featured the MBH99 hockey-stick figure and stated that it is "likely that, in the Northern Hemisphere, the 1990s was the warmest decade and 1998 the warmest year" in the past 1,000 years. MBH98 itself is cited in the broader literature as the origin of the multiproxy CFR approach that produced the hockey-stick shape for the last ~600 years. Later assessments and reviews frequently refer to the "MBH98/99" reconstructions collectively when discussing late-20th-century warmth relative to the prior centuries/millennium.

RECALLED (not used to anchor Field 5):
- The "hockey stick" visualization and the associated claim of late-20th-century warmth being exceptional relative to the preceding centuries became a central, widely restated emblem in policy, media, and assessment literature. Some secondary restatements blur the 1400 vs. 1000 boundary or attribute the full-millennium claim to the 1998 paper.

NONE FOUND (for exhaustive enumeration of every press release or every citing sentence): Searches targeted IPCC TAR text, major media of 1998, and common secondary attributions. Specific IPCC TAR text attributes the millennium claim primarily to the 1999 extension and related work; exact misattribution sentences assigning the 1000-year claim solely to MBH98 were not retrieved in this pass.

Verification notes: Attribution check for the core "three years warmer since 1400" claim shows the source itself supports it. Broader "warmest in 1000 years" or "millennium" restatements rest on MBH99 (or multi-study syntheses) and are therefore ATTRIBUTED ELSEWHERE when correctly cited; any downstream text that cites only MBH98 for a 1000-year claim would be MISATTRIBUTED (CROSS-SOURCE-CONFIRMED would be required to establish a specific instance). No such specific misattributing sentence was retrieved here.

Field 4 overall: partial — inflation analysis limited for the downstream component beyond media framing of the 1400 claim and the collective MBH98/99 reception. Distinction between "no downstream use of the exact quantified claim" vs. "retrieval limits on 1998-era press" cannot be fully resolved.

