6. WHICH CLAIM IS THIS AUDIT EVALUATING?
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The quantified claim from the source body: that the years 1990, 1995 and 1997 each show Northern Hemisphere mean annual temperature anomalies greater than any other year back to AD 1400 at 3 standard errors (~99.7% level of certainty), as reconstructed by the multiproxy EOF method.

Rationale for selection (Rule 2 — prefer quantified): This is the most precisely quantified version of the central warmest-years assertion. The abstract form lacks the explicit uncertainty quantification. Auditing this version tests whether the measurement and method support the stated quantity and confidence level. (If a different claim—e.g., the greenhouse-gas dominance attribution or a downstream millennium restatement—is preferred, a separate map should be run.)

This audit evaluates the SOURCE’S claim (#2 / quantified body version). Findings will concern the paper’s own operationalization and inference, not a downstream restatement.

